Silt REPL (type :quit to exit, :help for commands)
Commands:
  :help, :h      Show this help
  :quit, :q      Exit the REPL
  :type <expr>   Show the type of an expression without running it
  :doc <name>    Show the signature and docs of a builtin (list.map, Option, string) or of what an input declared or imported
  <Tab>          Autocomplete builtins and user-defined names

Enter expressions to evaluate, or declarations (fn, type, trait, import).
Multi-line input: an open brace, paren, bracket, string or block comment, or a line that ends in an operator (+, |>, =, -> ...), continues on the next line.
A brace in a string starts an interpolation: write \{ for the character itself.
